          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Proportional Reasoning–2"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "index": 1,
          "bbox": [
            0.407,
            0.101,
            0.59,
            0.126
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "SUMMARY"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 2,
          "bbox": [
            0.179,
            0.142,
            0.822,
            0.201
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Ratios in the form a : b : c : d : … indicate that for every a units of the first quantity, there are b units of the second quantity, c units of the third quantity, and so on."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 3,
          "bbox": [
            0.179,
            0.209,
            0.823,
            0.285
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "If x is divided into many parts in the ratio p : q : r : s : …, then the quantity of the first part is "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\chi \\times \\frac{p}{(p + q + r + s + \\cdots)}"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " , the quantity of the second part is "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "X \\times { \\frac { q } { (   p + q + r + s + \\cdots ) } }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " , and so on."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 4,
          "bbox": [
            0.179,
            0.29,
            0.823,
            0.412
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Two quantities are directly proportional when they both change by the same factor, and their quotient remains the same. For example, if x and y are two quantities that are directly proportional, and "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "( x _ { 1 } , x _ { 2 } , x _ { 3 } , \\ldots )"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " and "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "( y _ { 1 } , y _ { 2 } , y _ { 3 } , \\ldots )"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " are the corresponding values of x and y, then "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\frac{x_{1}}{y_{1}}=\\frac{x_{2}}{y_{2}}=\\frac{x_{3}}{y_{3}}=\\cdots=k,"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " where k is a constant."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 5,
          "bbox": [
            0.178,
            0.422,
            0.822,
            0.539
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Quantities are inversely proportional if, when one quantity changes by a factor n, the other quantity changes by the inverse "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\frac { 1 } { n }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " . For example, if x and y are two quantities that are inversely proportional, and "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\left( X_{1},X_{2},X_{3},\\cdots \\right)"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " and "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "( y _ { 1 } , y _ { 2 } , y _ { 3 } , \\ldots )"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " are the corresponding values of x and y, then "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "X_{1}y_{1}=X_{2}y_{2}=X_{3}y_{3}=\\cdots=n,"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " where n is a constant."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "page_number",
          "index": 6,
